        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c1_offline_reinforcement_learning_domai",
          "text": "Offline reinforcement learning in domains like healthcare and education must estimate the environment's transition dynamics from fixed batch data, yet standard maximum likelihood estimates give high variance policies that make dangerous mistakes where data is sparse.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "offline",
            "reinforcement",
            "learning",
            "domains",
            "like",
            "healthcare",
            "education",
            "must",
            "estimate",
            "environment"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c2_introduces_bayesian_inverse_transiti",
          "text": "This paper introduces Bayesian Inverse Transition Learning, a gradient free, constraint based method that uses an expert's near optimal demonstrations to clip a Bayesian posterior over the transition dynamics.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "introduces",
            "bayesian",
            "inverse",
            "transition",
            "learning",
            "gradient",
            "free",
            "constraint",
            "based",
            "method"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c3_result_distribution_dynamics_guarant",
          "text": "The result is a distribution of dynamics that guarantees safe, high performing policies, recovering one hundred percent accuracy on states where the best action is known and cutting policy variance dramatically across datasets.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "result",
            "distribution",
            "dynamics",
            "guarantees",
            "safe",
            "high",
            "performing",
            "policies",
            "recovering",
            "one"
          ],
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "id": "problem",
      "heading": "Problem",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c1_fields_like_healthcare_education_can",
          "text": "In fields like healthcare and education we cannot experiment freely, so offline reinforcement learning must learn the environment's transition dynamics purely from a fixed batch of collected experience.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "fields",
            "like",
            "healthcare",
            "education",
            "cannot",
            "experiment",
            "freely",
            "offline",
            "reinforcement",
            "learning"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_trouble_only_covers_actions_original",
          "text": "The trouble is that this data only covers the actions the original users actually took, leaving much of the state and action space unseen.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "trouble",
            "only",
            "covers",
            "actions",
            "original",
            "users",
            "actually",
            "took",
            "leaving",
            "much"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_standard_maximum_likelihood_estimate",
          "text": "Standard maximum likelihood estimates of the dynamics therefore produce policies that swing wildly from dataset to dataset and can recommend genuinely unsafe actions in the regions where data is thin.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "standard",
            "maximum",
            "likelihood",
            "estimates",
            "dynamics",
            "therefore",
            "produce",
            "policies",
            "swing",
            "wildly"
          ],
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "id": "motivation",
      "heading": "Motivation",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c1_key_insight_people_who_generate",
          "text": "The key insight is that the people who generate this offline data, such as clinicians, are usually acting near optimally.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "key",
            "insight",
            "people",
            "who",
            "generate",
            "offline",
            "such",
            "clinicians",
            "usually",
            "acting"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c2_their_choices_quietly_encode_which",
          "text": "Their choices quietly encode which actions are good and which are bad, yet a plain maximum likelihood fit of the dynamics throws that information away.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "their",
            "choices",
            "quietly",
            "encode",
            "which",
            "actions",
            "good",
            "which",
            "bad",
            "yet"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_earlier_gradient_based_inverse_reinf",
          "text": "Earlier gradient based inverse reinforcement learning methods try to recover an expert's belief about the dynamics, but they never connect their estimate back to the true environment and they suffer from the fragility of gradient optimization.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "earlier",
            "gradient",
            "based",
            "inverse",
            "reinforcement",
            "learning",
            "methods",
            "try",
            "recover",
            "expert"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c4_want_exploit_expert_signal_directly",
          "text": "We want to exploit the expert signal directly and without gradients.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "want",
            "exploit",
            "expert",
            "signal",
            "directly",
            "without",
            "gradients"
          ],
          "required": true
